<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soga clan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th–7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soga clan was a powerful aristocratic lineage of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamato-court">Yamato court</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the 6th and 7th centuries. Its leaders, Soga no Iname and Soga no Umako, championed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> after its arrival from Baekje and married their daughters into the royal line, dominating the court for generations. Their power ended in 645 when Prince Naka no Ōe and Nakatomi no Kamatari killed Soga no Iruka, opening the way to the Taika reforms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soga-clan.jpg" alt="Soga clan" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saigen Jiro · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sogatsuhiko-jinja,_haiden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
